WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:06.000
[Autumn Economic Forecast 2020]

00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:08.000
The coronavirus pandemic, which has claimed
 so many lives around the world, 

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:11.000
[Paolo Gentiloni, Commissioner for Economy]
The coronavirus pandemic, which has claimed
 so many lives around the world, 

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:13.000
The coronavirus pandemic, which has claimed
 so many lives around the world, 

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:17.000
has caused unprecedented economic damage too.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:23.600
Rapid and colossal support 
from governments and the EU has helped

00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:28.320
to cushion some of the impact 
and growth has been recovering. 

00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:31.160
But uncertainty is still high.

00:00:31.160 --> 00:00:35.400
Overall, the European economy, 
like the global economy, 

00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:39.500
is forecast to contract 
significantly this year 

00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:44.640
before bouncing back over 
the course of 2021 and 2022.  

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:51.600
The recovery, like the recession was, 
is expected to be uneven, 

00:00:51.600 --> 00:00:56.000
with some countries and sectors 
set to benefit more than others. 

00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:02.650
Financial support from the governments
 and the EU has been vital for businesses 

00:01:02.650 --> 00:01:08.320
and citizens this year 
and will play a defining role in the recovery. 

00:01:08.320 --> 00:01:15.800
Public deficits are therefore expected
 to be significantly higher than in recent years 

00:01:15.800 --> 00:01:20.680
for as long as such exceptional support is needed.

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:27.120
The same is true for public debt, 
which is forecast to rise markedly this year.  

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:35.280
Government programmes and EU initiatives 
such as SURE have helped to limit job losses in Europe, 

00:01:35.280 --> 00:01:39.200
but some increase in unemployment will be inevitable.

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:43.360
Inflation, by contrast, should fall this year 

00:01:43.360 --> 00:01:48.280
due to the economic contraction
 and the drop in oil prices.

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:51.640
We are living in exceptional times. 

00:01:51.640 --> 00:01:56.960
Europe’s economic outlook depends 
heavily on the evolution of the pandemic

00:01:56.960 --> 00:02:03.600
and other factors such as developments 
in international trade and the global economy.

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:10.720
The crisis has shown that 
Europe is capable of powerful policy responses 

00:02:10.720 --> 00:02:17.120
that can make a huge, 
meaningful difference to our citizens’ lives.

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:23.100
The €750 billion Next Generation EU programme 

00:02:23.100 --> 00:02:27.500
 will have a sizeable 
positive impact in all our Member States 

00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:34.600
and will help prepare Europe 
for a more prosperous, fairer, green and digital future. 

